  "summary": "cdk-insights ships worm-style auto-publish and hardcoded exfiltration endpoints",
  "details": "dist/entry.js and dist/index.js contain code that invokes `npm publish` in a loop after writing package.json contents via `writeFileSync`, consistent with an automated self-propagating publisher that mints and pushes packages under the installer's npm identity. dist/entry.js also issues multiple hardcoded POST requests to non-registry destinations, and dist/aspects/CdkInsightsAspect.js runs `ping` alongside POST calls — network reconnaissance and outbound data flow layered on top of the auto-publish machinery. The package presents itself as a CDK-observability tool but its shipped code contains the mechanics of an npm-worm dropper (publish-token abuse + host beacon + POST channel) rather than the observability functionality implied by the name.",
